# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS — never commit these.
# backend/.env holds ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, TWITTERAPI_IO_KEY and, on testnet,
# TREASURY_SIGNER_PRIVATE_KEY. Committing it publishes a key that can spend the
# treasury. `.env.example` is the file that belongs in the repo; `.env` never is.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# USER DATA — the bot's database maps X user IDs to wallet addresses.
# That is personal data and operational state; it does not belong in git.
# (SQLite in WAL mode also writes -wal and -shm sidecar files.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEPENDENCIES & BUILD OUTPUT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Hardhat / solc caches. contracts-test/artifacts.json is deliberately NOT
# ignored — it is the checked-in compile output the contract tests load.
cache/
artifacts/
typechain/
typechain-types/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOGS & SCRATCH
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.tmp
pons-factory-abi.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EDITOR / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
*.swp
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLAUDE CODE
#
# settings.local.json records machine-specific absolute paths and per-machine
# permission grants, so it stays local.
#
# .claude/skills/ is third-party tooling installed into this working copy
# (ui-ux-pro-max and friends) -- 8.5 MB and ~180 files of somebody else's code,
# each carrying its own licence. It is not part of Ponsr, it is not needed to
# build or run anything here, and vendoring it would republish other people's
# work under this repo. Install skills locally instead.
#
# CLAUDE.md and .claude/launch.json ARE committed: the first is this project's
# own context, the second is how the dev server is started.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/skills/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NETLIFY — .netlify holds the machine's link to the deployed site (site id and
# local state). Added by `netlify sites:create`; it is per-machine, not source.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.netlify

# Review artifacts, regenerated on demand from the branch itself.
#
# Never committed: a bundle or patch that lives inside the diff it describes changes
# that diff, so the artifact and its own hash can never agree.
#
# Patterns rather than the three literal filenames this started as. Those covered
# exactly the artifacts that existed the day they were written, so the first variant --
# `ponsr-current-v2-full.bundle`, a --all bundle made for the same review -- landed as
# untracked and dirtied the tree again. A rule that only knows yesterday's filenames
# fails on the next one, and the next one is always about to be made.
#
# `*.bundle` is deliberately broad: a git bundle is a copy of the repository's own
# history, so there is no version of "commit it into that repository" that makes sense.
*.bundle
ponsr-*-review.patch
ponsr-*-commits.txt
